{
  "$comment": "🎚️ What a dragged inline slider costs, as rows. A press is a run of `setSlider` sub-operations carrying ONE gesture id; the document must end on the value the user released on, and the whole press must fold into ONE undoable edit. Language-agnostic: the Rust law is `✏️editor/🎮️commands/✏️node-graph-edit/🧪️tests/🔬️unit`, the host half's twin is `📺️renderer/🧑‍🎨engine/🧪️tests/🎚️continuous-gesture-lane`. See `📓️slider-preview-update-2026-09-15.md`.",
